Zoom homogeneous box with GEAR sinks
=====================================

The gas box of examples/SinkParticles/HomogeneousBox, with dark matter added,
sits at the centre of a larger periodic box and runs as a zoom region
(--zoom). Background dark matter particles (PartType2) fill the rest of the
box in nested levels, as in a MUSIC zoom IC. The example covers two
geometries:

- a box of the order of the zoom region (default: 8 gas boxes);
- a box much larger than the zoom region, up to hundreds of Mpc or more
  comoving, with a small zoom region at its centre.

Build
-----

./configure --disable-mpi --with-chemistry=GEAR_10 --with-cooling=grackle_0 \
  --with-stars=GEAR --with-star-formation=GEAR --with-feedback=GEAR \
  --with-sink=GEAR --with-kernel=wendland-C2 --with-grackle=path/to/grackle
make -j

Sinks do not run with MPI. Build and run without MPI.

Run
---

run.sh makes the ICs, fetches the cooling and chemistry tables and runs
../../../swift. Set its variables on the command line:

  ./run.sh                                       # level 5 with sinks, 8 threads
  level=3 padding=2 n_threads=2 time_end=0.1 ./run.sh   # local test
  with_star_formation=1 ./run.sh                 # GEAR star formation instead of sinks
  level=8 n_threads=72 snapshot_delta=0.05 extra_params="-P Restarts:delta_hours:2" ./run.sh
  box_size=3.5 ./run.sh                          # box of 4 gas boxes (3.49 kpc)
  cosmological=1 ./run.sh                        # comoving ICs, --cosmology
  cosmological=1 box_size=100 levelmin=-6 ./run.sh      # 100 comoving Mpc box
  level=3 box_size=1000 levelmin=-12 n_threads=2 time_end=0.1 ./run.sh  # 1 Mpc box, no cosmology

Variables (default in brackets):

  level [5]           levelmax: 2^(3 level) gas particles in the gas box
  levelmin [level-3]  coarsest background level (see "Levels")
  padding [8]         cells of each coarser level around the finer one
  box_size [8 L]      box side: physical kpc, or comoving Mpc with
                      cosmological=1; L is the gas box side
  n_threads [8], gas_mass [50 Msun], jeans_length [0.25], dm_ratio [5.36],
  delta [0], with_star_formation [0], cosmological [0]
  time_end [0.5]      end time in internal units (cosmological=0)
  a_end_factor [2]    a_end / a_begin (cosmological=1)
  snapshot_delta [0.01]        time between snapshots (cosmological=0)
  snapshot_delta_cosmo [1.02]  ratio of scale factors between snapshots,
                               > 1 (cosmological=1)
  velocity_fraction [0.1]      random velocities (cosmological=1)
  max_bkg_cdim [91]   cap on ZoomRegion:bkg_top_level_cells
  swift [../../../swift], extra_params []  more -P options for swift

run.sh chooses the snapshot spacing from the cosmological flag.
"python3 makeIC.py --help" lists all IC options; "python3 makeIC.py
--dry-run ..." prints the layout and the zoom grid without writing a file.

Levels
------

The levels are those of MUSIC, counted from the gas box: level l has the
particle spacing L / 2^l.

- levelmax (level): the gas box, 2^level gas particles per dimension and
  as many PartType1 particles. The mean gas spacing d = L / 2^level is
  27.2 pc at 50 Msun for every level; L grows as 2^level (218 pc at level
  3, 872 pc at level 5, 6976 pc at level 8).
- Levels levelmax - 1 down to levelmin hold PartType2 on jittered
  lattices. Each level is a cube that contains the next finer one plus
  `padding` cells of its own spacing on each side (MUSIC "padding", default
  8). One cell is added on each side when needed, so that the cube has a
  multiple of 4 cells and its faces stay on the lattice of the next coarser
  level (MUSIC aligns its grids to 2 cells for the same reason). The mass
  per particle grows by 8 from one level to the next.
- levelmin may be 0 or negative (spacing L, 2 L, ...). The default
  levelmin = level - 3 gives spacings 2 d, 4 d and 8 d.
- The coarsest level that fits in the box fills the box. If the box is
  smaller than the padded region of levelmin, fewer levels are used. If it
  is larger, the coarsest level fills the remaining volume with a constant
  spacing.
- The box side is rounded to the nearest box with a whole, symmetric number
  of cells of the coarsest level (steps of 2 cells). makeIC.py prints the
  real box, the levels, the counts, the masses and the softenings.
- makeIC.py stops if the background needs more than 1e8 PartType2
  particles (--max-background-particles) and prints the levelmin that
  fills the box with padded levels only. A large box needs this levelmin:
  for example -5 for 100 comoving Mpc at level 5.

With the defaults the box is 8 L. At level 5 the 3 levels have 32 cells
across 2 L, 4 L and 8 L (28672 PartType2 each). At level 3, padding=2
gives the same layout (448 PartType2 per level): with padding 8 the second
level would need a box of 14 L.

  level  gas = PartType1  PartType2 (box 8 L)  L [pc]  box [pc]
  3      512              1344 (padding 2)      218     1744
  5      32768            86016                 872     6976
  8      16777216         17889088              6976    55805

Zoom grid
---------

makeIC.py writes zoom_runtime_params.txt, and run.sh passes it to swift
with -P. makeIC.py repeats the geometry of zoom_region_init()
(src/zoom_region/zoom_init.c) with the extent E of the gas and PartType1
particles, and stops with the reason if SWIFT would stop:

- ZoomRegion:region_pad_factor: 1.3. The zoom region is the block of
  background cells that holds the centred cube of side 1.3 E.
- ZoomRegion:bkg_top_level_cells: the value of the automatic mode of SWIFT
  (the largest odd number of cells with the padded zoom region inside one
  cell), capped at 91. The cap keeps the background grid at 753571 cells,
  about 1.4 GB (struct cell and its multipole, 1888 bytes), and lets the
  r_cut_max rule below hold with a mesh of 512. SWIFT stops if the zoom region
  is 64 times smaller than its block of background cells and warns at 16;
  makeIC.py does the same. Without the cap, a large box would need
  hundreds of cells per side.
- ZoomRegion:zoom_top_level_depth: the largest depth (at least 1) with zoom
  cells wider than 1.1 kernel_gamma SPH:h_max, at most 32 zoom cells per
  axis (--max-zoom-cdim) and zoom cells not narrower than a cell of the
  largest mesh (512, --max-mesh).
- Gravity:mesh_side_length: the smallest power of 2 (at least 16) with mesh
  cells not wider than a zoom cell (SWIFT stops otherwise at the first
  rebuild) and the tree cut-off r_cut_max = 4.5 x 1.25 box / mesh not
  larger than one background cell, so that background cells exchange tree
  forces only with their direct neighbours. The mesh does not need to
  resolve the gas box: the tree covers the zoom region. With the default
  box the mesh is 32 at level 3, 64 at level 5 and 256 at level 8.

In a large box the largest mesh sets the zoom cell: it is at least
box / 512, so the gas box can sit inside a few zoom cells (for 100
comoving Mpc at level 5: zoom cells of 3.68 physical kpc, gas box of
0.87 kpc). The usual cell tree then splits these cells.

makeIC.py --h-max MUST equal SPH:h_max. run.sh passes the same value to
both.

Large boxes and cosmology
-------------------------

With cosmological=1, makeIC.py writes comoving ICs and box_size is in
comoving Mpc. a_begin makes the mean matter density of the box equal to
Omega_m rho_crit_0, and the box follows the Hubble flow. With the default
densities a_begin = 0.0136 (z = 72.5). The gas box is then 0.872 physical
kpc (64.1 comoving kpc) at level 5. Examples (makeIC.py --dry-run):

  box [cMpc]  level  levelmin  real box [cMpc]  physical box  gas boxes  PartType2
  100         5      -6        98.49            1.339 Mpc     1536       364544
  1000        7      -9        984.9            13.39 Mpc     3840       1012648

For 1000 cMpc at level 5 the zoom region is 130 times smaller than one
background cell, and makeIC.py stops: raise --max-bkg-cdim (to at least
185) or the level.

Without cosmology, box_size is in physical kpc and the same rules hold.

SWIFT stops on zero velocities in cosmological runs, so the cosmological
ICs get Gaussian random velocities with a dispersion per component of
velocity_fraction (default 0.1) times the gas sound speed: 0.011 km/s at
level 3 and 0.042 km/s at level 5. This keeps the gas subsonic.
makeIC.py also writes the Cosmology block, the comoving softenings, the
comoving h_max and the output times to zoom_runtime_params.txt.

Density contrast
----------------

delta = rho_in / rho_out - 1 sets the total density outside the gas box.
With delta = 0 (default) the whole box is uniform. With delta > 0 the gas
box is an overdensity: outside, the background follows
rho(r) = rho_out + (rho_in - rho_out) (1 - tanh((r - L/2) / w)),
with r the max-norm distance from the centre and w = 0.25 L. The gas stays
a sharp cube. With cosmological=1 the mean of the box is the cosmological
mean, so in a large box rho_out is close to Omega_m rho_crit_0 / a_begin^3.

Softening
---------

- Gas, stars, sinks and PartType1: 5 pc (Gravity:max_physical_baryon_softening
  and max_physical_DM_softening).
- PartType2: Gravity:softening_ratio_background = 0.05 times the mean
  spacing of particles of its mass at the mean matter density of the box,
  the usual value of the zoom examples. This gives 2.72, 5.45 and 10.9 pc
  for the spacings 2 d, 4 d and 8 d at 50 Msun, and twice as much for each
  coarser level. makeIC.py prints the values and writes the ratio to
  zoom_runtime_params.txt.

Gas particle mass
-----------------

gas_mass sets the gas particle mass in Msun (default 50), for example:

  gas_mass=100 level=3 padding=2 n_threads=2 time_end=0.1 ./run.sh

The gas density stays 0.1 atom/cm^3. With s = (gas_mass / 50)^(1/3):

- The gas box side L, the mean spacing and h (1.2348 times the spacing)
  grow as s.
- run.sh passes SPH:h_max = 0.08 s kpc to makeIC.py and to swift, so the
  zoom grid stays the same as for 50 Msun.
- run.sh passes max_physical_baryon_softening and max_physical_DM_softening
  = 0.005 s kpc and, with sinks, GEARSink:cut_off_radius = 0.005 s kpc. A
  sink forms only where kernel_gamma h < cut_off_radius, so the density at
  which sinks can form stays the same.

The parameter files hold the values for 50 Msun. run.sh overrides them, so
change these values in run.sh, not in the parameter files.

These values do not scale with the gas mass: the density and temperature
thresholds of sink and star formation, the time-step limits, the feedback
parameters, stellar_particle_mass_Msun and the spare particles per cell
(Scheduler block).

Initial temperature: at fixed jeans_length it grows as L^2, so it grows
with the level and as gas_mass^(2/3). It is 16 K at level 5 and about
1000 K at level 8 (50 Msun). To keep the temperature of level 5, scale
jeans_length as 1/L: 0.03125 at level 8.

How it is built
---------------

- Gas (PartType0): uniform random positions in a cube of side L, density
  0.1 atom/cm^3, zero velocity without cosmology. The internal energy
  u = sigma^2 uses the velocity dispersion of the original example (set by
  jeans_length).
- Dark matter (PartType1): one particle per gas particle. Each pair comes
  from one random point, split as in space_generate_gas() (src/space.c).
  The dark matter density is dm_ratio times the gas density (default 5.36,
  the Planck 2018 ratio of cold dark matter to baryons). The free-fall time
  of the gas box is 65 Myr (0.066 internal units).
- Background dark matter (PartType2): the levels above. No PartType2
  particle is inside the gas box.

Parameter files: params_sinks.yml (--sinks) and params_star_formation.yml
(--star-formation). The physics blocks are the ones of
examples/SinkParticles/HomogeneousBox/params.yml.
